SCD tells us what to do when data changes — replace it, keep it, or store part of it.

SCD1-> Overwrites existing data and does NOT maintain history
SCD2-> Maintains full history by adding new rows 
SCD3-> Maintains limited history (only previous value)

NOTE:
SCD2 WILL ACHEIVE IN MULTIPLE APPROCHES
->SINGLE STEP APPROCH
->TWO STEP APPROCH
->2LEFTSEMI AND 2 LEFTANTI IN PYSPARK 

SINGLE STEP APPROCH:-
One statement → easy to maintain
Optimized by engine → faster
When to use:
Using Delta Lake / Databricks / modern warehouses
Tables are large
Need better performance
Want clean and simple code

SECOND STEP APPROACH:-
Need more control/debugging
Small-to-medium datasets
Easy to understand
Step-by-step visibility

LEFTSEMI/LEFTANTI:-
Need custom complex logic
Want to control data transformations manually
Full control over logic
